WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.935
Video nine. A sales invoice with GST, and its
print.

00:00:05.135 --> 00:00:08.553
One sales invoice sends each amount to its
ledger.

00:00:08.483 --> 00:00:12.300
Sharma Traders owes you ₹53,025.

00:00:12.231 --> 00:00:15.847
₹50,500 go to the Sales Account.

00:00:15.777 --> 00:00:22.527
The tax goes to CGST and SGST, half each. Your
GST return takes it from there.

00:00:22.827 --> 00:00:28.177
V opens the vouchers. F8 is Sales. It opens in
Item Invoice mode.

00:00:28.207 --> 00:00:33.956
Select the party, Sharma Traders, and the
sales ledger. The place of supply is Gujarat.

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:39.785
Type "cotton", and press Enter. Hisaab asks
for the godown.

00:00:39.815 --> 00:00:44.300
Ring Road Warehouse: 100 metres, at 180
rupees.

00:00:45.002 --> 00:00:50.685
Enter on End of List. The line shows ₹18,000,
with GST at 5%.

00:00:50.715 --> 00:00:55.998
Click the next line for the second item: silk,
50 metres at 650 rupees.

00:00:57.746 --> 00:01:00.896
Below the items, select the tax ledgers.

00:01:00.926 --> 00:01:08.876
CGST, then SGST. Hisaab calculates each one:
₹1,262.50.

00:01:08.906 --> 00:01:15.323
Type the narration. The total is ₹53,025.
Hisaab asks: Accept?

00:01:16.403 --> 00:01:22.685
Y for yes. Now the bill-wise details: a new
reference, bill 1, due in 30 days.

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:25.067
Ctrl+A saves the invoice.

00:01:26.817 --> 00:01:29.300
Page Up opens the invoice again.

00:01:29.765 --> 00:01:36.917
Ctrl+P shows the print preview: a tax invoice with both
GSTINs, the HSN codes, and the amount in words.

00:01:36.947 --> 00:01:44.099
P prints. In the Windows app, the print window shows a
preview. Choose the printer there, or Save as PDF.

00:01:44.579 --> 00:01:48.329
One invoice: ₹53,025.

00:01:48.259 --> 00:01:52.475
₹2,525 of it is GST.

00:01:52.676 --> 00:01:56.226
Next: a purchase from another state, and the
bills.

